WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:10.580
46. A Mixed New World. It's morning in the not-too-distant future.

2
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:16.620
You wake up. You shoot some virtual aliens in your kitchen while eating breakfast. Later,

3
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.900
you take your virtual pet dinosaur out for a walk in the park. And when you get home,

4
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.980
you realize you don't like the way you've decorated your apartment. Easily fixed. With

5
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:33.520
a few waves of your hand, your home now resembles a grand European palace. That's better.

6
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:41.160
Welcome to the exciting world of mixed reality. Defining exactly what mixed reality, MR is,

7
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:48.640
can be tricky. Is it the same as virtual reality, VR? What about augmented reality, AR? How

8
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:56.280
is MR different from that? Basically, VR shuts out the real world and wraps the user completely

9
00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:02.720
in a virtual one. AR, on the other hand, takes the user's view of the real world and adds

10
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:09.880
digital information to it. An example of AR is the game Pokemon Go. You can see the creatures

11
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:16.440
against a real world background, but they can't interact with it. MR is somewhere in between. As

12
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:24.040
an AR, digital images are placed over the real world. But in MR, these images can interact with

13
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:29.680
that world as if they themselves were real. Imagine that the Pokemon you were hunting could

14
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:36.840
hide behind cars or climb up trees. To make this possible, the real world environment first has to

15
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:44.640
be mapped using 3D cameras. This allows the virtual images to know where they are in it. The user

16
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:52.200
wearing a headset can then see the two worlds, real and virtual, as one. MR is set to become

17
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:58.840
the technology of the near future, and the possible applications are truly vast. Everything

18
00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:05.880
from gaming to communications to medicine will be changed by MR. So, get ready. Reality, as we

19
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.960
know it, is about to get a full virtual makeover.
